=== invariants_dst (D7, invariant-set/1) ===
  i 13 families (D7's twelve, plus ADR-003 D4's journal fold):
      terminal-summary: exactly one final RunSummary for every SystemRun, and none synthesized for a harness failure
      emission-parity: parity between all logical ledger emissions and returned trace records
      phase-transitions: legal phase/state transitions
      tool-pairing: valid tool-call/tool-result pairing, including denial and failure paths
      budget-accounting: monotonically valid budget/cost accounting
      bounded-progress: bounded retry and progress behavior under the modeled fault catalogue
      checkpoint-history: checkpoint/compaction history invariants already owned by the framework
      outcome-agreement: agreement between returned outcome and terminal summary
      replay-consistency: strict-replay request equality, safe regression-replay compatibility, and complete interaction consumption
      world-transitions: valid logical-world transitions, including declared commit/no-commit behavior under faults
      virtual-time: monotonic virtual time and deadline derivation
      harness-hygiene: zero discovery-generator failures, matcher mismatches, forbidden effects, and ambient RNG reads
      journal-fold: a fold of the run's journal-class records reproduces the state the run ended holding, field by field

-- the surviving fixture --
  ✓ the fixture satisfies all 13 families
  ✓ invariants_ok agrees
  ✓ first_failed_invariant is None on a clean run

-- S7: the surviving fixture carries every shape the specification protects --
  ✓ all 11 D2 interaction classes appear
  ✓ all three outcome statuses appear (ok=17 fault=3 missing=1)
  ✓ all three tool fault classes appear
  ✓ chunks appear on one provider interaction and not the other
  ✓ both deadline sentinels appear (-1 on a deadline-free class, 0 and a positive on deadline-bearing ones)
  ✓ the approval channel carries a denial and an end-of-input, and neither call is dispatched
  ✓ the returned trace carries all three LedgerRecord constructors

-- S7: no two of the surviving fixture's quantities are equal --
  ✓ 11 named quantities, pairwise distinct

-- D6.4: the parity register, and the reclassification it forbids --
